{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFound in the Step 7 parity census for bug `5931-78a3-95d2-44cd`. On Jira Data Center the\noutbound comment send path applies **no length fit at all**, so an over-length comment is\nhanded to Jira unfitted. Bug `6afc-20ee-84e5-4dd5` established Jira exits 0 on an\nover-length rejection, so the comment never lands and is re-emitted every pass — the\noutbound comment-sync loop. DC's ceiling is deployment-resolved (`comment_max_chars()`,\nbug `049e`) and typically low, so an unfitted DC body is MORE likely to be rejected.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/_links.py` `_CommentsMixin.add_comment` passes `body`\n  straight to `self._client.add_comment`; `JiraDataCenterBackend.add_comment` is a bare\n  delegate to it.\n- `_DCSanitizer.sanitize_comment` — the send-side sanitizer with its operator warning —\n  has **no production caller** (grep hits are test files only). The same is true for\n  Cloud's `_JiraSanitizer.sanitize_comment`.\n- `fit_comment` (the differ-side twin) IS wired via `outbound_comments._diff_comments`:\n  the comparison half of the convergence pair is live, the SEND half is not.\n- NOT bug 5931's mechanism (Cloud truncated and lost the marker); DC does not truncate\n  at all — the mirror-image gap.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **Fit the DC send path, reusing the existing marker-preserving fitter — no second\n  fitter.** Wire `_DCSanitizer.sanitize_comment` into `JiraDataCenterBackend.add_comment`\n  (the one production caller of the transport's `add_comment`, covering all three\n  enactment sites), and recompose `sanitize_comment` so its injected `truncate` is\n  `outbound_comments.fit_preserving_marker` over the existing `_truncate_dc_comment_body`\n  at the `comment_max_chars()` ceiling — the composition Cloud's send path uses in\n  `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` (commit 6724e79e8f). A marker-less body goes straight to the\n  raw fit, so existing `sanitize_comment` behaviour on undecorated bodies stays\n  byte-identical (049e ceiling tests pass unchanged). Ceiling resolution is untouched.\n- **Keep the dedup key synchronized with what lands (the class commit 103729e90c fixed\n  for Cloud).** Re-derive `_DCSanitizer.fit_comment` via\n  `outbound_comments.fit_comment_as_sent` over the same raw fit — the marker-stripped\n  body the fitted send actually lands — mirroring Cloud's post-e339 `fit_comment`. Both\n  sides change in this one change. In-limit bodies return byte-identical.\n- **Cloud's dead `sanitize_comment` is REMOVED, not wired.** Cloud's live send fit is\n  `fit_preserving_marker(body, AdfCodec.fit_outbound)` (measures SERIALIZED ADF); the\n  dead method applies a plain 32,767-char cap that would cut the RECONCILER_MARKER if\n  ever wired — the false assurance the AC names. Remove `_JiraSanitizer.sanitize_comment`,\n  its delegate `jira_fields._sanitize_comment`, the `acli.py` facade re-export, and the\n  `FieldSanitizer.sanitize_comment` protocol member (nothing calls it through the port;\n  DC keeps its concrete, now-wired method — a Protocol permits extra members).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` — recompose `sanitize_comment`\n  (marker-preserving), re-derive `fit_comment` (as-sent), wire `add_comment`.\n- `adapters/jira/backend.py`, `adapters/jira/jira_fields.py`, `adapters/jira/acli.py`,\n  `_backend.py` — remove the dead Cloud `sanitize_comment` chain + protocol member.\n- `outbound_comments.py` — `fit_comment_as_sent` docstring: no longer Cloud-only.\n- Tests: NEW `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_send_path_comment_fit.py`; update\n  `test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py`'s convergence test to the as-sent contract; remove\n  the Cloud `sanitize_comment` characterization tests in\n  `test_backend_characterization.py`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- **RED (wiring):** build `JiraDataCenterBackend` over the REAL transport (`_links.py`\n  mixins) with a stubbed jira client recording the body it receives; send an\n  over-ceiling RECONCILER_MARKER-decorated body through `backend.add_comment`; assert\n  the wire body is `<= comment_max_chars()` and still ends with the marker. Fails\n  pre-fix, passes post-fix.\n- **RED (dedup-key):** for the same over-length body, `sanitizer.fit_comment(user_body)`\n  equals the marker-stripped wire body captured from the send path (the e339 class).\n- **Edges:** an in-limit decorated body passes through byte-identical; a `0` (unlimited)\n  ceiling passes an over-stock-length body through untouched.\n- Existing suites stay green: `test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py`,\n  `test_dc_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py`, `test_dc_backend_characterization.py`,\n  `test_backend_characterization.py`, `diffing/`, `mutate/`.\n- Verify: targeted `pytest -q` over the files above, then `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n  `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The DC outbound send path fits comment bodies to the deployment-resolved ceiling —\n      checked: new send-path test asserts the transport-client-captured wire body\n      length is `<= comment_max_chars()`.\n- [ ] The RECONCILER_MARKER survives the DC fit via the reused `fit_preserving_marker` —\n      checked: the same test asserts the captured wire body ends with the marker.\n- [ ] The new send-path test is RED on pre-fix code — checked: run it against the\n      unmodified tree and observe the failure before committing the fix.\n- [ ] `_DCSanitizer.fit_comment` equals the marker-stripped body the fitted send lands\n      (e339 dedup-key consistency) — checked: the new consistency test and the updated\n      049e convergence test pass.\n- [ ] Cloud's `sanitize_comment` is removed (rationale in Approach) — checked:\n      `grep -rn \"def sanitize_comment\" src/rebar | grep -qv jira_datacenter | grep -qv\n      jira_family; test $? -ne 0` (only the DC implementation and the shared\n      `jira_family` helper remain).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, the targeted pytest selection, and\n      `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` all exit 0 in the worktree."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787335225109817001,"uuid":"21794f8d-b367-4b92-bb84-32d5a4f695b2"}